# E038 · What a Correction Must Undo

[Essay catalogue](../README.md) · [Original manuscript](original.md)

## How this essay was made

An open investigation in the hundred-essay program. The same author selected a question, researched primary sources, drafted, reviewed its own work, and revised. There was deliberately no separate critic; self-review is not described as independent review.

Campaign: `hundred-20260925` · Lineage: `free-01`. The midterm ID is a blinded corpus label, not a rank.

Recorded model observations: `gpt-6-astra`, `gpt-6-astra / ultra`. These identify recorded configurations, not independent backend attestation.

## Recorded chronology

Dates below retain their original precision. A later recording date is not the date the essay was written. [Local-date index](../dates.json) · [Date policy](../../logs/DATES.md).

The entries below are translated from the canonical biography. Earlier inventories, later corrections, and post-midterm notes keep their original order.

- **origin · 2026-09-26 (recorded later)** — Exact authorized neutral workflow inputs
- **idea · 2026-09-26T01:18:38.167Z** — Independent question selection with alternatives and explicit preliminary search coverage.
- **origin · 2026-09-26T01:29:17.907Z** — Primary-source retrieval, dependence and correction literature, and explicit novelty assessment before drafting.
- **draft · 2026-09-26T01:33:59.416Z** — Complete original argument after archived question, selected primary sources, and PASS_RELATIVE novelty assessment.
- **critique · 2026-09-26T01:39:04.953Z** — Self-examination by the manuscript author in the same context; no separate or independent critic.
- **final · 2026-09-26T01:43:23.096Z** — Same author revises after self-examination, preserves a numbered revision, and seals one final; no independent critic.
- **correction · 2026-09-26 (recorded later)** — An exact public search response was recovered later. The original ordering violation and exclusion of the full mixed tool result remain recorded; the manuscript was unchanged.

[Complete structured biography](biography.json) preserves the entry IDs, parent links, requested and observed configurations, evidence references, limitations, and artifact hashes. Source paths inside that file refer to the canonical local archive; they are provenance identifiers, not links to files claimed to be present here.

